BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the passive voice with modal perfects \(Must have been, Could have been, Should have been\) in retrospective audit reports.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Role in Quality Assurance and GLP Audits:) Tj
T*
(   Retrospective bio-manufacturing audits \(FDA 21 CFR Part 11, cGMP\) investigate batch) Tj
T*
(   contamination, deviations from standard operating procedures, and clinical data integrity) Tj
T*
(   failures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Diagnostic Modal Perfect Passives:) Tj
T*
(   - Must have been + V3 \(Definitive Historical Deduction\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The cold-chain storage unit must have been unplugged during the weekend maintenance cycle,) Tj
T*
(   causing thermal denaturation of the viral vaccines.") Tj
T*
(   - Should have been + V3 \(Unfulfilled SOP Protocol / Non-Compliance\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The bioreactor pressure relief valve should have been calibrated on October 14; failure to) Tj
T*
(   do so violated safety protocols.") Tj
T*
(   - Could have been + V3 \(Alternative Counterfactual Prevention\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The bacterial contamination could have been prevented if an in-line 0.22-micrometer sterile) Tj
T*
(   filter had been installed.") Tj
T*
(   - Might have been + V3 \(Unresolved Hypothesis\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The anomalous chromatogram peak might have been caused by residual mobile-phase impurities.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 19:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the stylistic peril of 'Passive Stacks' \(chained passive clauses\) and demonstrate sentence disentangling.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Pathology of the Passive Stack:) Tj
T*
(   Novice scientific writers often chain multiple passive verbs within a single sentence, burying) Tj
T*
(   causal agency, inflating word count, and paralyzing syntactic flow:) Tj
T*
(   - Pathological Passive Stack: "It was decided that the culture should be harvested, and an) Tj
T*
(   extraction of the proteins was attempted to be performed by the researchers.") Tj
T*
(   - Diagnosis: Three passive constructions \('was decided', 'should be harvested', 'was attempted) Tj
T*
(   to be performed'\) suffocating a simple procedure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Disentangling and Syntactic Re-Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Identify the true human agent and key physical actions.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Recast the main decision in active voice while retaining objective passive for) Tj
T*
(   procedural steps where appropriate:) Tj
T*
(   - Streamlined Revision A: "The researchers decided to harvest the culture and extract total) Tj
T*
(   cellular proteins.") Tj
T*
(   - Streamlined Revision B \(Methodological Focus\): "The culture was harvested, and total cellular) Tj
T*
(   proteins were extracted via ultrasonic lysis.") Tj
T*
(   - Impact: Enhances clarity, reduces cognitive fatigue, and restores energetic momentum.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 20:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze modal verbs of deduction in interpreting negative controls and experimental anomalies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Logic of Scientific Deduction:) Tj
T*
(   In interpreting biochemical assays, researchers evaluate control lanes to deduce the) Tj
T*
(   operational validity of the entire system:) Tj
T*
