T*
(   2. Modal Formulations in Control Interpretation:) Tj
T*
(   - Deduction of Contamination \(Positive Signal in Negative Control\):) Tj
T*
(   - "Because the non-template control lane produced a bright 500 bp band, the PCR master mix must) Tj
T*
(   be contaminated with exogenous plasmid template." \(High certainty; 'must be'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Deduction of Reagent Failure \(Negative Signal in Positive Control\):) Tj
T*
(   - "Because the positive control failed to fluoresce, the primary antibody must have lost its) Tj
T*
(   binding activity.") Tj
T*
(   - Deduction of Impossibility \(Cannot / Can't\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The observed 25 kDa band cannot be the full-length recombinant fusion protein, which has a) Tj
T*
(   calculated molecular weight of 72 kDa." \(Logical impossibility\).) Tj
T*
(   - Tentative Inference \(May / Might\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The faint band at 25 kDa may represent a proteolytic degradation fragment or an alternative) Tj
T*
(   splice variant.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 21:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the syntax of 'Need' and 'Dare' as marginal modal auxiliaries versus lexical main verbs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Dual Grammatical Identity:) Tj
T*
(   'Need' and 'Dare' function both as modal auxiliaries \(taking a bare infinitive without 'to',) Tj
T*
(   lacking third-person -s inflection, taking negative 'not' directly\) and as ordinary lexical) Tj
T*
(   main verbs \(taking 'to'-infinitive, third-person -s, and requiring 'do'-support\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Modal Auxiliary Usage \(Formal, Negative Contexts\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The technician need not autoclave pre-sterilized filter tips." \(Modal: no -s, bare) Tj
T*
(   infinitive 'autoclave', negated with 'not'\).) Tj
T*
(   - "How dare the investigator publish unverified clinical trial data?" \(Modal inversion\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Lexical Main Verb Usage \(Standard Modern Syntax\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The technician does not need to autoclave pre-sterilized filter tips." \(Main verb: takes) Tj
T*
(   'do'-support and 'to'-infinitive\).) Tj
T*
(   - "The cells need to be incubated at 37 deg C." \(Passive infinitive complement\).) Tj
T*
(   - Stylistic Note: Modern technical English predominantly uses the lexical verb form \("does not) Tj
T*
(   need to"\), while the modal form \("need not"\) persists in formal institutional directives.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 22:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the passive voice in describing flowcharts, manufacturing pipelines, and bioprocess engineering flow.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Process Description Syntax:) Tj
T*
(   Describing industrial bioprocesses \(e.g., monoclonal antibody manufacturing, beer brewing,) Tj
T*
(   recombinant insulin production\) requires depicting an unbroken sequence of automated and) Tj
T*
(   physical transformations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Chronological Cohesion with Passive Chains:) Tj
T*
(   Deploying passive voice with transitional chronological markers \(initially, subsequently,) Tj
T*
(   thereafter, following this, finally\) establishes objective, factory-floor procedural) Tj
T*
(   continuity:) Tj
T*
(   - "Initially, the genetically engineered Chinese Hamster Ovary \(CHO\) cells are inoculated into) Tj
T*
(   seed bioreactors.") Tj
T*
(   - "Upon reaching target cell density, the culture is transferred into a 5,000-liter production) Tj
T*
ET

