BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the modal 'Would' in describing past laboratory routines, prospective designs, and polite discourse.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Multi-Faceted Roles of 'Would':) Tj
T*
(   - Role 1: Past Habitual Action in Retrospective Histories:) Tj
T*
(   - Describes regular, repeated procedures performed in past eras:) Tj
T*
(   - "In early molecular biology laboratories, researchers would routinely pour sequencing gels) Tj
T*
(   manually between large glass plates.") Tj
T*
(   - Role 2: Hypothetical Consequence in Conditional Frameworks:) Tj
T*
(   - "Eliminating the C-terminal domain would destabilize the catalytic core.") Tj
T*
(   - Role 3: Tentative Proposal / Softened Assertion:) Tj
T*
(   - "We would argue that current vector designs are suboptimal for in vivo targeting." \(Softens) Tj
T*
(   authorial assertion\).) Tj
T*
(   - Role 4: Polite Requests in Academic Correspondence:) Tj
T*
(   - "We would be grateful if you could share the hybridoma clone for non-commercial academic) Tj
T*
(   research.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 24:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the passive transformation of verbs taking that-clause complements and infinitive raising.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Two Syntactic Passivization Strategies for Verbs of Cognition:) Tj
T*
(   Verbs of cognition, reporting, and belief \(think, believe, report, know, consider, demonstrate,) Tj
T*
(   prove, expect\) governing a 'that'-clause can be passivized via two distinct syntactic) Tj
T*
(   operations:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Strategy A: Impersonal Passive with Expletive 'It':) Tj
T*
(   - Active: "Scientists believe that the gut microbiome influences neurological health.") Tj
T*
(   - Impersonal Passive: "It is believed that the gut microbiome influences neurological health.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Strategy B: Subject Raising \(Personal Passive with Infinitive\):) Tj
T*
(   - The subject of the subordinate 'that'-clause is raised to become the grammatical subject of) Tj
T*
(   the passive matrix verb:) Tj
T*
(   - Raised Passive: "The gut microbiome is believed to influence neurological health.") Tj
T*
(   - Applied Scientific Example with Past Perfect / Anteriority:) Tj
T*
(   - Active: "Researchers reported that the virus had mutated prior to the outbreak.") Tj
T*
(   - Raised Passive: "The virus was reported to have mutated prior to the outbreak." \(Notice:) Tj
T*
(   perfect infinitive 'to have mutated' preserves anterior chronology\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
