(   In contemporary spoken and academic English, 'shall' has virtually disappeared as a) Tj
T*
(   first-person future marker, replaced universally by 'will'.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Specialized Bastion of 'Shall': Legal Contracts & Patent Claims:) Tj
T*
(   In regulatory frameworks \(FDA, EMA\), international treaties, and patent claims, 'shall' carries) Tj
T*
(   immense, legally binding deontic force:) Tj
T*
(   - Mandatory Patent Requirement: "The lyophilized formulation shall contain between 5% and 10%) Tj
T*
(   trehalose by weight.") Tj
T*
(   - Legal Meaning: A formulation with 4.9% trehalose falls outside patent coverage; 'shall') Tj
T*
(   establishes strict legal boundary conditions.) Tj
T*
(   - Statutory Regulatory Compliance: "The sponsor shall submit annual safety reports to the) Tj
T*
(   regulatory authority.") Tj
T*
(   - Meaning: Absolute legal obligation; failure constitutes a statutory offense.) Tj
T*
() Tj
