/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the avoidance of passive voice with reciprocal verbs and non-passivizable idioms in technical discourse.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Non-Passivizable Verbs in English:) Tj
T*
(   Not all transitive verbs that take direct objects can be transformed into passive voice:) Tj
T*
(   - Verbs of Possession and Relationship: have, possess, resemble, fit, suit, lack:) Tj
T*
(   - Active: "The mutant plasmid lacks an ampicillin resistance cassette.") Tj
T*
(   - Ungrammatical Passive: "*An ampicillin resistance cassette is lacked by the mutant plasmid.") Tj
T*
(   - Active: "The cloned gene resembles human hemoglobin.") Tj
T*
(   - Ungrammatical Passive: "*Human hemoglobin is resembled by the cloned gene.") Tj
T*
(   - Reciprocal Verbs:) Tj
T*
(   - Active: "The two helical strands interlock." \(Cannot be passivized without shifting to) Tj
T*
(   transitive agentive form\).) Tj
T*
(   - Idiomatic Prepositional Collocations:) Tj
T*
(   - "The experiment took place yesterday." \(*Yesterday was taken place by the experiment is) Tj
T*
(   ungrammatical\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the modal verb 'Used to' versus 'Would' in historical accounts of biotechnological breakthroughs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Morphological and Semantic Contrast:) Tj
T*
(   Both 'used to' and 'would' express repeated past habits that are no longer true, but they) Tj
T*
(   diverge in important syntactic constraints:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Past Habits vs. Past States:) Tj
T*
(   - 'Used to' describes BOTH past repeated actions AND past permanent states:) Tj
T*
(   - Past State: "Biotechnology companies used to believe that small molecules were superior to) Tj
T*
(   biologic therapeutics." \(Correct\).) Tj
T*
(   - Ungrammatical with Would: "*Biotechnology companies would believe that small molecules were) Tj
T*
(   superior." \('Would' cannot describe past stative beliefs\).) Tj
T*
(   - 'Would' describes strictly repeated dynamic actions, and typically requires an explicit past) Tj
T*
(   temporal anchor:) Tj
T*
(   - "In the 1970s, whenever researchers synthesized oligonucleotides, they would spend days) Tj
T*
(   purifying them on polyacrylamide gels.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Editorial Choice:) Tj
T*
(   Use 'used to' to contrast obsolete theoretical paradigms with modern realities; deploy 'would') Tj
T*
(   to narrate historical procedural routines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 30:) Tj
T*
