(   [Problem Statement]: Synthesize guidelines for achieving stylistic harmony between active voice, passive voice, and modal hedging in a doctoral dissertation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Rhetorical Symphony of a Dissertation:) Tj
T*
(   A doctoral thesis in biotechnology is an advanced scientific argument requiring a calibrated) Tj
T*
(   blend of active agency, objective passivity, and epistemic modesty:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Section-by-Section Best Practices:) Tj
T*
(   - Abstract & Title: Active and direct. State the core finding immediately: "Here, we show) Tj
T*
(   that...") Tj
T*
(   - Introduction: Active voice when positioning your doctoral hypothesis against literature;) Tj
T*
(   passive when summarizing broad established scientific paradigms.) Tj
T*
(   - Materials and Methods: 85-90% agentless passive voice to ensure total methodological) Tj
T*
(   objectivity and universal reproducibility; active voice only when detailing novel customized) Tj
T*
(   protocols.) Tj
T*
(   - Results: Balanced alternation. Passive for procedural setups \("Cells were treated with) Tj
T*
(   compound 4b"\); Active for observational outcomes \("The compound elicited a 3-fold reduction in) Tj
T*
(   viability; Figure 3 illustrates this trend"\).) Tj
T*
(   - Discussion & Conclusions: Modals and hedging become paramount \(may, could, should, suggest,) Tj
T*
(   indicate\) to interpret biological implications with scholarly rigor, avoiding dogmatic) Tj
T*
(   over-claiming while actively defending authorial interpretations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

